#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gh-shim: the `gh` operations the hakuX harness uses, served by the local forge.

GitHub suspended the harness account on 2026-09-29 and every `gh` call has
returned 403 since. Most callers send gh's stderr to /dev/null and read an
empty stdout as "nothing to do", so the harness went quiet instead of
failing. This executable sits earlier on PATH than /usr/bin/gh and answers
the same command lines from the local Forgejo (127.0.0.1:3330,
docs/lanes/localforge/NOTES.md).

Rules it keeps:
  * It FAILS LOUDLY. Any error exits nonzero with one stderr line naming the
    operation. It never turns a failure into empty success.
  * An operation it does not implement exits 64 with
    "gh-shim: not implemented: <args>". So do flags it does not know.
  * Every call is logged, one JSON line, to $GH_SHIM_LOG
    (default ~/hakux-work/logs/forge/shim.log). That log is how a missing
    operation shows up.
  * The repo is --repo/-R, else $GH_REPO, else jreinach-alt/hakuX. The forge
    has an org of that name, so the default slug needs no translation.
  * The account is $FORGE_USER, else it follows $HAKUX_ROLE (lane and cloud
    map to `lanes`), else `jobs`. Its token is $FORGE_TOKENS/<user>.token.
  * Output follows gh's shapes:
    - `--json` field names, with uppercase states.
    - `--jq` runs through jq -r -c, so strings come out raw and objects
      compact.
    - `gh api` returns the REST body. GitHub-only endpoints (check-runs,
      issue events, comment sort order) are synthesised from Forgejo's.
    - Timestamps are UTC, ending in Z.
  * Drafts are Forgejo's work-in-progress title prefix ("WIP: "). The prefix
    is stripped from titles on output and set by `pr create --draft` and
    `pr ready --undo`.
  * `pr merge` is refused: merges go through offline-git/foldqueue.sh, and
    a forge-only commit would be overwritten by the next hakux-forge-sync.
"""
